version: "2.0"
description: >-
  Gnomon wrapper — Gnomon.app, the Tauri 2 shell (Rust over WKWebView) that is
  the GUI's default daily surface (docs/specs/gnomon.md §11.1, §11.2 rule 2,
  §16, §18; M1.13, P8-D56). Slice 1 is macOS; WebView2 and the native
  capture-exclusion panel (S29-K8, M4.6) are later phases with seams left.

components:
  gnomon-wrapper:
    description: >-
      Package-level component (allowlisted in packages/gnomon/test/symbol-allowlist.json:
      Appendix A treats gnomon-wrapper as a package, not a spec node). Tauri
      pinned exact (=2.12.4; tauri-build =2.7.3). One window whose main frame
      is in exactly one phase the NATIVE side moves (src/nav.rs): the bundled
      status page (tauri://localhost) or the one kernel origin
      http://127.0.0.1:<port>; on_navigation refuses every other URL (another
      port, localhost, userinfo tricks, other schemes) and on_new_window
      denies. IPC is disabled for page content (src/surface.rs): invoke_system
      replaces Tauri's invoke script with a stub that holds no invoke key and
      throws, there is no command and no invoke handler, capabilities: [] (the
      generated gen/schemas/capabilities.json is {}), withGlobalTauri: false,
      freezePrototype: true. Devtools only in debug builds (no devtools
      feature). A document-start script defines a frozen
      window.gnomonSurface='wrapper' on the 127.0.0.1 origin only, which the
      GUI reads to declare hello surface wrapper and drop the extension-risk
      badge (display only). Hardened runtime with an EMPTY entitlements set.
      Double-click flow (src/main.rs): the app spawns `node --disable-sigusr1 <dist>/cli/gnomon.js
      up --wrapper` (src/kernel.rs: env_clear + HOME USER LOGNAME LANG TMPDIR
      SHELL + fixed PATH, no NODE_OPTIONS/GNOMON_*/DYLD_*). Trust root (Aegis
      C1, src/tree.rs shared with build.rs): the build records the node path
      as found plus the sha256 of its realpath target, and the
      gnomon-wrapper-kernel-tree:v1 hash of packages/gnomon/{dist,package.json};
      check_trust_root re-hashes both before every spawn and refuses "built
      against a different node/kernel … Rebuild the app" (covers brew upgrade
      node). local.signed.json is not a node source (Aegis C2). Stderr to
      ~/Library/Logs/Gnomon/kernel.log (0600), reads gnomon-wrapper-channel:v1
      (src/contract.rs; LaunchGrant Debug redacts token and key), and on a grant
      runs the native preflight (src/loopback.rs): channel bundleHash == the pin
      compiled from gui-bundle.ts (src/bundle.rs), its own WebSocket hello with
      surface wrapper verified natively (src/verify.rs: ed25519-dalek strict,
      exact SPKI, kernel keyId, sent clientNonce, gnomon:auth-server:v2), then
      every pinned file and / re-hashed — only then Phase::Kernel and navigate.
      Any refusal (unprovisioned shows `gnomon identity init`) stays on the
      status page. Window close hides (kernel keeps running), Dock click
      reopens, Cmd-Q sends quit, waits 10 s, kills. Tests: unit (nav, surface,
      contract, verify against TS-generated vectors, bundle, kernel env/argv),
      tests/live_kernel.rs (preflight vs a live dev kernel; a foreign key and
      another pin refused), tests/no_page_ipc.rs (config falsifiers).
      Round 2: the child is `node --disable-sigusr1 …` (NODE_FLAGS, first and
      only); the channel is #wrapper-channel; lines are capped at 64 KiB at
      read time; at stdout EOF the phase returns to Status and an EOF without
      a refusal/down line says "the kernel exited before starting" with the
      status; Cmd-Q prevent_exit + worker-thread stop (try_wait, 10 s, kill);
      src/logfile.rs opens kernel.log O_NOFOLLOW with fchmod/fstat checks and
      a 0700 dir; tests/crafted_ipc.rs (Tauri mock runtime: keyless messages
      dropped, keyed commands refused from both origins); subframes are
      excluded by the kernel CSP frame-src 'none' (falsified statically and
      on the live header). #setup-endpoint (T-2026-10-19-005 MVP-b): an
      unprovisioned home makes `up --wrapper` emit {t:setup,port,setupToken,
      setupPublicKey,bundleHash,expiresAt} (contract.rs SetupGrant, Debug
      redacted; ^setup-token exactly 43 base64url); loopback.rs
      setup_preflight runs the SAME pin and serverSig checks against the
      ephemeral setup key speaking gnomon-setup:v1; nav.rs Phase::Setup{port}
      locks navigation to that one origin; the page reaches no Tauri command
      (G-GUI-12). After success the channel's {t:up} continues into the
      normal launch. refusal_text no longer says "In Terminal". The bundled
      status page (static/status.css) uses the GUI's type tokens
      (--fs-reading, --fs-title) and base radius (--radius 3), see
      #gui-type and #gui-space-radius.
    path: src
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, wrapper, tauri, rust, paradigm-8, M1.13]
